{
 "about": "General universe knowledge loaded as store items: quantity kinds with dimensions, scale and lexical anchors (D2, D4), condition concepts and a method concept. Domain-free. Terms are lexical anchors only (the weakest anchor, never sufficient for identity, D4); which kind a term names is decided by the value's unit dimension. A term names a kind only for its exact meaning: generic kinds keep only generic terms, and a header whose words are not all explained leaves the content incomplete. I-2: kinds state whether they are a determinable of the bearer or only a dimension class, may declare the conditions that define the measurand, and may be spans whose limits are quantities of their own; part kinds, artefact kinds, condition values and a test standard are items too. Each is a lexical anchor only (the weakest, S0 3.6.5); what a header means is decided by the placement of all its words and the value's unit.",
 "provenance": {
  "source": "general metrology and scientific usage (JCGM 200:2012; SI Brochure 2019; S0 4.6, 4.7)",
  "holder": "developer",
  "basis": "definition"
 },
